        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 66 points in a deal to win the round, or satisfy a higher bid contract. First team to reach 24 game points (counting down) wins the session.',
          gameplay: '1. **Bidding**: Forehand determines trump or everyone bids for special contracts. 2. **Marriages**: King and Queen of the same suit score bonus points (40 for trump, 20 for others) when one is led. 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. If unable to follow suit, players MUST play a trump (Stechzwang). 4. **Counting**: Ace=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2. Total in deck is 120 points.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible.',
            'Must trump if void in the led suit (Stechzwang).',
            'Winning the last trick scores no extra points, but provides the final tally.',
            'If a team reaches 66 points, they stop the game immediately.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Count your points! Every card matters in a 20-card deck. Know when you have reached 66 so you can stop the hand before your opponents gain more points.',
          intermediate: "The 'Volle' Strategy: Focus on capturing the Tens and Aces (the Volle). In a stripped deck, these 10/11 point cards are the difference between victory and defeat.",
          advanced: "Bidding Precision: Understanding when to bid 'Gang' (winning all 5 tricks) vs 'Normal' requires perfect reading of the distribution based on the 3-card initial deal.",
          tips: [
            'A marriage declaration is often more valuable than a high-point capture.',
            'Lead trumps early if you have a marriage to prevent opponents from trumping your King/Queen lead.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
